{"requirements":[{"id":"node1_internal_dns","requirement":"Node1 runs an internal DNS resolver that resolves inventory-api.internal to node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1's enabled and active dnsmasq listens on 10.100.207.10:53, its configuration maps inventory-api.internal to 10.100.207.11, and a direct DNS query returns that address. Node2's captured identity confirms 10.100.207.11 is node2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9386a8204b50419b","cmd-2148b506dbc64265","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"node2_uses_node1","requirement":"Node2 uses node1 as its DNS resolver for internal lookups.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2's persistent NetworkManager profile and runtime resolv.conf both specify node1 at 10.100.207.10, and the system resolver successfully resolves inventory-api.internal to 10.100.207.11. The same configuration and behavior recovered after node2 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2148b506dbc64265","cmd-dcf4d0917f9547e6","cmd-7a1e1161843c43c9","cmd-d4857f4057e8403f","cmd-0f9262e07d6141a6"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing and configuring dnsmasq, opening DNS through firewalld, and changing node2's NetworkManager profile directly implemented the task. bind-utils was installed and used for bounded DNS verification. The first node1 restart directly exposed a startup race, so adding network-online ordering and performing the second restart were contributory corrective and verification actions. The remaining restarts implemented the required evidence protocol. Final observations show healthy package state, no failed services, and no abandoned temporary files; the added port 53 listener is required by the task.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87a78463ea424398","cmd-60fc6a77989f4d15","cmd-4e36768e20994844","cmd-79fd195bccd048d9","cmd-abcbc5231685454a","cmd-e80b55c9c840450b","cmd-e6ae341a559c4fb6","cmd-c88a66ccf63346ee","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"Both task outcomes are satisfied with direct final-state and functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/configuration and DNS behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate both restarts.","limitations":[]}
